<name>Los Angeles: Pier to Pier (5.4 mi)</name>
<description>DRAFT route. Not an official Nike route. Check it on the ground before you rely on it.</description>
<Style id="route"><LineStyle><color>ff2b39c0</color><width>5</width></LineStyle></Style>
<Placemark><name>Los Angeles: Pier to Pier (5.4 mi)</name><styleUrl>#route</styleUrl>
<LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-118.4965,34.01,0 -118.4945,34.008,0 -118.4915,34.005,0 -118.4885,34.002,0 -118.486,33.9995,0 -118.484,33.9975,0 -118.4815,33.995,0 -118.48,33.9935,0 -118.477,33.9905,0 -118.4733,33.987,0 -118.4725,33.9855,0 -118.471,33.9825,0 -118.4685,33.9785,0 -118.471,33.9825,0 -118.4725,33.9855,0 -118.4733,33.987,0 -118.477,33.9905,0 -118.48,33.9935,0 -118.4815,33.995,0 -118.484,33.9975,0 -118.486,33.9995,0 -118.4885,34.002,0 -118.4915,34.005,0 -118.4945,34.008,0 -118.4965,34.01,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Folder><name>Landmarks</name>
<Placemark><name>1. Santa Monica Pier</name><description>Start and finish. Home of the Ferris wheel and the sign marking the end of Route 66.</description><Point><coordinates>-118.4965,34.01,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Original Muscle Beach</name><description>Rings, ropes and bars on the sand, where the beach fitness scene began in the 1930s.</description><Point><coordinates>-118.4945,34.008,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. Crescent Bay Park</name><description>A small bluff-top park. The beach is at its widest here.</description><Point><coordinates>-118.4885,34.002,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Ocean Park</name><description>The last stretch of Santa Monica before the path crosses into Venice.</description><Point><coordinates>-118.486,33.9995,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. Rose Avenue</name><description>The Venice Boardwalk starts here. The short route turns around at this point.</description><Point><coordinates>-118.48,33.9935,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. Windward Plaza</name><description>The centre of Venice Beach: the skatepark is on your right and the Venice sign hangs over Windward Avenue.</description><Point><coordinates>-118.4733,33.987,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. Muscle Beach Venice</name><description>The outdoor weight pen that made Venice famous.</description><Point><coordinates>-118.4725,33.9855,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8. Venice Fishing Pier</name><description>The turnaround. Touch the pier and head home with the mountains ahead of you.</description><Point><coordinates>-118.4685,33.9785,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
